[{:db/id 17592186133891 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ca5fbd9d-06c2-5516-a2aa-caaa1b2a1fc6"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133892 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2f9d1bf2-2ca6-5610-aed1-5f5054aae288"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133893 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ada3d128-ac86-51c2-88c8-3e672e4cad88"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-ca5fbd9d-06c2-5516-a2aa-caaa1b2a1fc6" :question/id #uuid "ca5fbd9d-06c2-5516-a2aa-caaa1b2a1fc6" :question/math-academy-id "q-124246" :question/problem "![](images/88/88da0f1ddf1f605186c9d921a9eade24b5f0aa9de2ae4afdc51a921586093b16.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}x,$ where $C$ is the path along the line segment from the point $(-2,3)$ to the point $(0,0),$ as shown above?\n\n*Hint: Use the parametrization $r(t)=⟨2t-2,\\,3-3t⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ is a line segment with endpoints $(-2,3)$ and $(0,0).$ It can be parametrized as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨(-2+t(0-(-2))),\\,(3+t(0-3))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t-2,\\,3-3t⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$\n\nComputing $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t-2)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)={x}^{2}y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =(2t-2)^{2}(3-3t) \\\\  & =4(t-1)^{2}\\cdot 3(1-t) \\\\  & =-12(t-1)^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}-12(t-1)^{3}\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-24{\\int }_{0}^{1}(t-1)^{3}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d86ee8d9-aeae-5ab1-b4a0-98c765570dca"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d86ee8d9-aeae-5ab1-b4a0-98c765570dca" :answer-field/id #uuid "d86ee8d9-aeae-5ab1-b4a0-98c765570dca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5550e6c3-7324-5809-9dfc-0f8be5c60c9e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-78816eec-e214-5a4a-a51d-fa5102203d98" "answer-5550e6c3-7324-5809-9dfc-0f8be5c60c9e" "answer-1b787a8e-ad68-5398-92d2-2ebf1e8be534" "answer-02ba6004-1436-5e5b-ae2f-735e7eb45f4f" "answer-9756d62a-6b6c-5317-a183-008b9c4d2660"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-78816eec-e214-5a4a-a51d-fa5102203d98" :answer/id #uuid "78816eec-e214-5a4a-a51d-fa5102203d98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-12{\\int }_{0}^{1}(t-1)^{3}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5550e6c3-7324-5809-9dfc-0f8be5c60c9e" :answer/id #uuid "5550e6c3-7324-5809-9dfc-0f8be5c60c9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-24{\\int }_{0}^{1}(t-1)^{3}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1b787a8e-ad68-5398-92d2-2ebf1e8be534" :answer/id #uuid "1b787a8e-ad68-5398-92d2-2ebf1e8be534" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2t-1)^{3}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-02ba6004-1436-5e5b-ae2f-735e7eb45f4f" :answer/id #uuid "02ba6004-1436-5e5b-ae2f-735e7eb45f4f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24{\\int }_{0}^{1}(t-3)^{3}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9756d62a-6b6c-5317-a183-008b9c4d2660" :answer/id #uuid "9756d62a-6b6c-5317-a183-008b9c4d2660" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2t-1)^{3}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2f9d1bf2-2ca6-5610-aed1-5f5054aae288" :question/id #uuid "2f9d1bf2-2ca6-5610-aed1-5f5054aae288" :question/math-academy-id "q-124272" :question/problem "![](images/f5/f5f5b235b54d2acd20297ab365d9b93907111b3fec9a86776c28e93fdfe105ee.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y,$ where $C$ is the path along the line segment from the point $(0,0)$ to the point $(2,3),$ as shown above?\n\n*Hint: Use the parametrization $r(t)=⟨2t,\\,3t⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ is a line segment with endpoints $(0,0)$ and $(2,3).$ It can be parametrized as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨(0+t(2-0)),\\,(0+t(3-0))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,3t⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$\n\nComputing $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t)=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =(2t)^{2}+(3t)^{2} \\\\  & =4{t}^{2}+9{t}^{2} \\\\  & =13{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}13{t}^{2}\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =39{\\int }_{0}^{1}{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2c3bc565-6668-5708-9572-740391604ada"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2c3bc565-6668-5708-9572-740391604ada" :answer-field/id #uuid "2c3bc565-6668-5708-9572-740391604ada" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f113768c-cf48-5fce-945b-53b72f33cbc9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8b05db23-972c-567b-8223-11bddcab9b32" "answer-25e50d33-12b9-5c12-ac4e-4e3135ef41df" "answer-a18fa886-a66f-5c1c-a378-38efae13d666" "answer-f113768c-cf48-5fce-945b-53b72f33cbc9" "answer-92ad03ae-93a6-5758-8869-8e58634200a0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8b05db23-972c-567b-8223-11bddcab9b32" :answer/id #uuid "8b05db23-972c-567b-8223-11bddcab9b32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13{\\int }_{0}^{1}(3{t}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-25e50d33-12b9-5c12-ac4e-4e3135ef41df" :answer/id #uuid "25e50d33-12b9-5c12-ac4e-4e3135ef41df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13{\\int }_{0}^{1}{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a18fa886-a66f-5c1c-a378-38efae13d666" :answer/id #uuid "a18fa886-a66f-5c1c-a378-38efae13d666" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "26{\\int }_{0}^{1}(3{t}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f113768c-cf48-5fce-945b-53b72f33cbc9" :answer/id #uuid "f113768c-cf48-5fce-945b-53b72f33cbc9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "39{\\int }_{0}^{1}{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-92ad03ae-93a6-5758-8869-8e58634200a0" :answer/id #uuid "92ad03ae-93a6-5758-8869-8e58634200a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9{\\int }_{0}^{1}(3-{t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ada3d128-ac86-51c2-88c8-3e672e4cad88" :question/id #uuid "ada3d128-ac86-51c2-88c8-3e672e4cad88" :question/math-academy-id "q-124172" :question/problem "![](images/09/09a38bb4306728f97b7fecbf9ab1bda7aa957607352c1ab27af09489c271c3ed.png)\n\nEvaluate ${\\int }_{C}({y}^{2}-2x)\\,\\text{d}y,$ where $C$ is the path traversed along the line segment from the point $(0,1)$ to the point $(2,3),$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nThe curve $C$ is a line segment with endpoints $(0,1)$ and $(2,3).$ It can be parametrized as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨(0+t(2-0)),\\,(1+t(3-1))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,1+2t⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$\n\nComputing $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+2t)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)={y}^{2}-2x$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =(1+2t)^{2}-2(2t) \\\\  & =1+4t+4{t}^{2}-4t \\\\  & =4{t}^{2}+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(4{t}^{2}+1)\\cdot 2\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1}(4{t}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2{[\\frac{4{t}^{3}}{3}+t]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2(\\frac{4}{3}+1)-2(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8b9c47c5-4e96-58fa-ac91-5791dc11f30c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8b9c47c5-4e96-58fa-ac91-5791dc11f30c" :answer-field/id #uuid "8b9c47c5-4e96-58fa-ac91-5791dc11f30c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6029d8a7-a6ae-5959-9ee4-f8e3ebd8e072" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c94fc212-35ff-5e38-9f57-12d4f4959a4c" "answer-6029d8a7-a6ae-5959-9ee4-f8e3ebd8e072" "answer-21702398-6680-552d-923f-027dff95a35a" "answer-ea8f272e-677d-5489-96d8-1e29db88e990" "answer-78ae96ca-4942-5362-807b-c0b65d2496c2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c94fc212-35ff-5e38-9f57-12d4f4959a4c" :answer/id #uuid "c94fc212-35ff-5e38-9f57-12d4f4959a4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6029d8a7-a6ae-5959-9ee4-f8e3ebd8e072" :answer/id #uuid "6029d8a7-a6ae-5959-9ee4-f8e3ebd8e072" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{14}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-21702398-6680-552d-923f-027dff95a35a" :answer/id #uuid "21702398-6680-552d-923f-027dff95a35a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ea8f272e-677d-5489-96d8-1e29db88e990" :answer/id #uuid "ea8f272e-677d-5489-96d8-1e29db88e990" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-78ae96ca-4942-5362-807b-c0b65d2496c2" :answer/id #uuid "78ae96ca-4942-5362-807b-c0b65d2496c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186135122 :tutorial/content "Until now, we've been dealing with line integrals with respect to arc length. In this lesson, we will learn about other types of line integral. \n\nSuppose that $C$ is a path in the $xy$-plane with initial point $A$ and terminal point $B.$ The line integral of the function $f(x,y)$ **with respect to $\\boldsymbol x$** along the path $C$ is denoted\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nTo understand what this integral represents, we imagine traversing $C$ from $A$ to $B.$ At each point $P$ that lies on $C,$ we project the point on $f$ that lies directly above $P$ onto the plane $y=0.$ Doing this for every point on $C$ traces out a curve. The line integral of $f$ with respect to $x$ gives the (signed) area bounded by this curve and the $x$-axis.\n\n![](images/62/62c07a36cbf79459021ee7be125536a8f9c1bc3c193a99eabfcd3fc851b8eb0c.png)\n\nTo calculate a line integral with respect to $x,$ we must first parameterize $C$ using a parameter $t\\in [a,b].$ Then, we apply the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n\\int\\limits_C f(x, y) \\, \\textrm{d}x  = \\int\\limits_a^b  f(\\mathbf r(t)) \\, \\dfrac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} \\, \\textrm{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nLet's take a look at a concrete example." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133995 :activity/expected-seconds 900.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162107 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c60b1a3b-1eee-5254-929b-6a532b619fd6"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-c60b1a3b-1eee-5254-929b-6a532b619fd6" :question/id #uuid "c60b1a3b-1eee-5254-929b-6a532b619fd6" :question/math-academy-id "q-143431" :question/problem "A sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2}$ of two pineapples is drawn from a population. The population has pineapples of two different weights, $1\\,\\text{kg}$ and $1.5\\,\\text{kg},$ distributed in the ratio $1:4.$ Calculate the standard error of $\\overset{―}{X}.$ Round your answer to two decimal places." :question/worked-solution "If ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sample of size $n$ from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population variance ${\\sigma }^{2},$ then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\mu ,\\,\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n},\n$$\n\nand the standard error is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{SE}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}]}=\\frac{\\sigma }{\\sqrt{n}}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that the pineapples in the population have weights $1\\,\\text{kg}$ and $\\text{1.5}\\,\\text{kg},$ and these are distributed in the ratio $1:4.$ Therefore, to compute the population's mean and variance, we can consider a population consisting of $1+4=5$ pineapples only with the following weights:\n\n$$\n1\\,\\text{kg},\\,1.5\\,\\text{kg},\\,1.5\\,\\text{kg},\\,1.5\\,\\text{kg},\\,1.5\\,\\text{kg}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the population mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mu  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\sum }_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(1+4\\cdot 1.5) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(1+6) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{5} \\\\  & =1.4\\,\\text{kg},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the population variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\sum }_{i}{x}_{i}^{2}-{\\mu }^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}({1}^{2}+4\\cdot {1.5}^{2})-{1.4}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(10)-1.96 \\\\  & =2-1.96 \\\\  & =0.04\\,{\\text{kg}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the sample size is $n=2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n}=\\frac{0.04}{2}=0.02\\,{\\text{kg}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\text{SE}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\sqrt{0.02}≈0.14\\,\\text{kg}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-784c4051-09fc-584b-bc9b-b914c96abf6f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-784c4051-09fc-584b-bc9b-b914c96abf6f" :answer-field/id #uuid "784c4051-09fc-584b-bc9b-b914c96abf6f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cbdd89a6-5722-5be8-bfb0-7a19c704530e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2b023dd3-5d4c-5904-81ba-d35305307de4" "answer-cbdd89a6-5722-5be8-bfb0-7a19c704530e" "answer-25766927-d6f2-5fbe-a0a7-d435805ace1e" "answer-e3d733c3-af8b-53a6-abf7-8e175451a049" "answer-35c2b0e9-3ebd-579b-8077-e6f35b16b833"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2b023dd3-5d4c-5904-81ba-d35305307de4" :answer/id #uuid "2b023dd3-5d4c-5904-81ba-d35305307de4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.04\\,\\text{kg}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cbdd89a6-5722-5be8-bfb0-7a19c704530e" :answer/id #uuid "cbdd89a6-5722-5be8-bfb0-7a19c704530e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.14\\,\\text{kg}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-25766927-d6f2-5fbe-a0a7-d435805ace1e" :answer/id #uuid "25766927-d6f2-5fbe-a0a7-d435805ace1e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.41\\,\\text{kg}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e3d733c3-af8b-53a6-abf7-8e175451a049" :answer/id #uuid "e3d733c3-af8b-53a6-abf7-8e175451a049" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.40\\,\\text{kg}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-35c2b0e9-3ebd-579b-8077-e6f35b16b833" :answer/id #uuid "35c2b0e9-3ebd-579b-8077-e6f35b16b833" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.96\\,\\text{kg}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119859 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7c3f2557-93da-5d6b-97fe-29c0805f0db0"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-7c3f2557-93da-5d6b-97fe-29c0805f0db0" :question/id #uuid "7c3f2557-93da-5d6b-97fe-29c0805f0db0" :question/math-academy-id "q-75975" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember, the order of the vectors in a basis is important.\n\nNotice that \n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}={{(\\,6\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{1}}+{{(\\,-3\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{2}}\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\nx=6\\cdot {b}_{1}+(-3)\\cdot {b}_{2}\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we have that ${x}_{2}=-3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7bb29f16-8d05-55d0-ab1d-19d482085ecc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7bb29f16-8d05-55d0-ab1d-19d482085ecc" :answer-field/id #uuid "7bb29f16-8d05-55d0-ab1d-19d482085ecc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7700fc74-62d9-5c43-a14e-3089802b8f61" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7700fc74-62d9-5c43-a14e-3089802b8f61" "answer-d197d8cb-a53e-5fcb-9f95-86830c4ab9d9" "answer-9d1c50f8-8c07-5027-b319-7781b3d31cfe" "answer-afa06ac1-854a-5acd-a258-9948876f2387" "answer-e51a43de-aaa3-5ca0-b2ff-dd23d8bf03d4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7700fc74-62d9-5c43-a14e-3089802b8f61" :answer/id #uuid "7700fc74-62d9-5c43-a14e-3089802b8f61" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d197d8cb-a53e-5fcb-9f95-86830c4ab9d9" :answer/id #uuid "d197d8cb-a53e-5fcb-9f95-86830c4ab9d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d1c50f8-8c07-5027-b319-7781b3d31cfe" :answer/id #uuid "9d1c50f8-8c07-5027-b319-7781b3d31cfe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-afa06ac1-854a-5acd-a258-9948876f2387" :answer/id #uuid "afa06ac1-854a-5acd-a258-9948876f2387" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e51a43de-aaa3-5ca0-b2ff-dd23d8bf03d4" :answer/id #uuid "e51a43de-aaa3-5ca0-b2ff-dd23d8bf03d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186208843 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9c36f01c-b274-57ce-a233-5c5a47d4ef94"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-9c36f01c-b274-57ce-a233-5c5a47d4ef94" :question/id #uuid "9c36f01c-b274-57ce-a233-5c5a47d4ef94" :question/math-academy-id "q-274929" :question/problem "Given that $P$ is a $2\\times 5$ matrix, $Q$ is a $5\\times 7$ matrix, and $R$ is a $7\\times 2$ matrix, in which of the following expressions are the Hadamard products well-defined?\n\nI. $PQ⊙R$\n\nII. $PQ⊙{R}^{T}$\n\nIII. $(PQ)^{T}⊙R$" :question/worked-solution "The Hadamard product of two matrices (or vectors) is only defined if they have the same dimensions.\n\nLet's consider each expression in turn:\n\n- The dimensions of $PQ$ are $2\\times 7,$ and the dimensions of $R$ are $7\\times 2.$ Hence, the Hadamard product in expression I is *not* well-defined.\n\n- The dimensions of $PQ$ are $2\\times 7,$ and the dimensions of ${R}^{T}$ are $2\\times 7.$ Hence, the Hadamard product in expression II is well-defined.\n\n- The dimensions of $(PQ)^{T}$ are $7\\times 2,$ and the dimensions of $R$ are $7\\times 2.$ Hence, the Hadamard product in expression III is well-defined.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-06b8bf76-c702-59e2-a003-890dc8fb5ea1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-06b8bf76-c702-59e2-a003-890dc8fb5ea1" :answer-field/id #uuid "06b8bf76-c702-59e2-a003-890dc8fb5ea1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e220b7cd-3f24-57e9-9712-d0be4b086080" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0bf5a550-ab0e-57f9-9420-6f5fc19c9793" "answer-544ac095-1bdb-582c-b5a1-d915b8edf13e" "answer-e220b7cd-3f24-57e9-9712-d0be4b086080" "answer-de661f83-ea91-5ae2-a236-5063d72239bd" "answer-7e56ec3f-c043-5d3d-9ed2-fde627fa5136"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0bf5a550-ab0e-57f9-9420-6f5fc19c9793" :answer/id #uuid "0bf5a550-ab0e-57f9-9420-6f5fc19c9793" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-544ac095-1bdb-582c-b5a1-d915b8edf13e" :answer/id #uuid "544ac095-1bdb-582c-b5a1-d915b8edf13e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e220b7cd-3f24-57e9-9712-d0be4b086080" :answer/id #uuid "e220b7cd-3f24-57e9-9712-d0be4b086080" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-de661f83-ea91-5ae2-a236-5063d72239bd" :answer/id #uuid "de661f83-ea91-5ae2-a236-5063d72239bd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7e56ec3f-c043-5d3d-9ed2-fde627fa5136" :answer/id #uuid "7e56ec3f-c043-5d3d-9ed2-fde627fa5136" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198261 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2e5452f1-e9dc-544d-b364-2b179ccf8284"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-2e5452f1-e9dc-544d-b364-2b179ccf8284" :question/id #uuid "2e5452f1-e9dc-544d-b364-2b179ccf8284" :question/math-academy-id "q-183347" :question/problem "$\\,$ If $x\\in (0,2),$ then $|x|<2.$\n\nWhich of the following is logically equivalent to the conditional predicate above?" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote by $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ the following predicates:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x\\in (0,2).$\n\n- $Q(x):$ $|x|<2.$\n\nThen, our initial sentence can be written as $P(x)⇒Q(x),$ which is logically equivalent to \n\n$$\n¬P(x)∨Q(x).\n$$\n\nThe negation of $P(x)$ can be written as\n\n- $¬P(x):$ $x\\notin (0,2).$\n\nTherefore, the given sentence is logically equivalent to the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x\\notin (0,2),$ or $|x|<2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8a43a5f5-8ea0-5a0e-95e4-95914ae5bdd0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8a43a5f5-8ea0-5a0e-95e4-95914ae5bdd0" :answer-field/id #uuid "8a43a5f5-8ea0-5a0e-95e4-95914ae5bdd0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3f34cc74-45f1-5809-a233-34d9ed2b693c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b5a4df82-563a-51ab-aef5-2059ef4e092c" "answer-dca2faf0-be7b-54d7-8aa5-f4260d682846" "answer-4c23175b-7774-5cee-98b8-f552daf6d3a2" "answer-3f34cc74-45f1-5809-a233-34d9ed2b693c" "answer-0fced56e-d01f-5fd1-a5b9-535d61f4ce4c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b5a4df82-563a-51ab-aef5-2059ef4e092c" :answer/id #uuid "b5a4df82-563a-51ab-aef5-2059ef4e092c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x\\in (0,2),$ and $|x|<2.$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dca2faf0-be7b-54d7-8aa5-f4260d682846" :answer/id #uuid "dca2faf0-be7b-54d7-8aa5-f4260d682846" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x\\in (0,2),$ or $|x|<2.$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4c23175b-7774-5cee-98b8-f552daf6d3a2" :answer/id #uuid "4c23175b-7774-5cee-98b8-f552daf6d3a2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x\\notin (0,2),$ and $|x|<2.$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3f34cc74-45f1-5809-a233-34d9ed2b693c" :answer/id #uuid "3f34cc74-45f1-5809-a233-34d9ed2b693c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x\\notin (0,2),$ or $|x|<2.$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0fced56e-d01f-5fd1-a5b9-535d61f4ce4c" :answer/id #uuid "0fced56e-d01f-5fd1-a5b9-535d61f4ce4c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x\\notin (0,2),$ or $|x|\\ge 2.$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-36b6f9e9-f573-549e-9f71-6397aa6ad974" :activity/id #uuid "36b6f9e9-f573-549e-9f71-6397aa6ad974" :activity/title "Quiz 8" :activity/type :activity.type/assessment :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-59e78201-ec48-592f-9f5a-c19cf70fbfec" "step-83027d2b-c1b9-55ba-91ba-820e391ce4c9" "step-017b013a-5450-516d-883d-82ac20f6d367" "step-71f4128d-bc24-55af-9a46-51453e907aa2" "step-130bb05a-f55b-5271-9ddc-91048c211b25" "step-4e2187ca-5b58-5ec6-83a8-fd8d094052e7" "step-a6cb874c-0dc1-505f-b8a2-5ec8d9f951fa" "step-881f72c0-3118-514a-bf11-8e15d0a4f0d4"] :activity/first-step "step-59e78201-ec48-592f-9f5a-c19cf70fbfec" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-59e78201-ec48-592f-9f5a-c19cf70fbfec" :step/id #uuid "59e78201-ec48-592f-9f5a-c19cf70fbfec" :step/content "question-c60b1a3b-1eee-5254-929b-6a532b619fd6" :step/next "step-83027d2b-c1b9-55ba-91ba-820e391ce4c9" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-83027d2b-c1b9-55ba-91ba-820e391ce4c9" :step/id #uuid "83027d2b-c1b9-55ba-91ba-820e391ce4c9" :step/content "question-7c3f2557-93da-5d6b-97fe-29c0805f0db0" :step/next "step-017b013a-5450-516d-883d-82ac20f6d367" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-017b013a-5450-516d-883d-82ac20f6d367" :step/id #uuid "017b013a-5450-516d-883d-82ac20f6d367" :step/content 17592186368716 :step/next "step-71f4128d-bc24-55af-9a46-51453e907aa2" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-71f4128d-bc24-55af-9a46-51453e907aa2" :step/id #uuid "71f4128d-bc24-55af-9a46-51453e907aa2" :step/content 17592186406982 :step/next "step-130bb05a-f55b-5271-9ddc-91048c211b25" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-130bb05a-f55b-5271-9ddc-91048c211b25" :step/id #uuid "130bb05a-f55b-5271-9ddc-91048c211b25" :step/content 17592186371700 :step/next "step-4e2187ca-5b58-5ec6-83a8-fd8d094052e7" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-4e2187ca-5b58-5ec6-83a8-fd8d094052e7" :step/id #uuid "4e2187ca-5b58-5ec6-83a8-fd8d094052e7" :step/content "question-9c36f01c-b274-57ce-a233-5c5a47d4ef94" :step/next "step-a6cb874c-0dc1-505f-b8a2-5ec8d9f951fa" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-a6cb874c-0dc1-505f-b8a2-5ec8d9f951fa" :step/id #uuid "a6cb874c-0dc1-505f-b8a2-5ec8d9f951fa" :step/content "question-2e5452f1-e9dc-544d-b364-2b179ccf8284" :step/next "step-881f72c0-3118-514a-bf11-8e15d0a4f0d4" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-881f72c0-3118-514a-bf11-8e15d0a4f0d4" :step/id #uuid "881f72c0-3118-514a-bf11-8e15d0a4f0d4" :step/content 17592186348198 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068800 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-504684ef-507d-57b1-81c3-7c9672d3e28f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-504684ef-507d-57b1-81c3-7c9672d3e28f" :question/id #uuid "504684ef-507d-57b1-81c3-7c9672d3e28f" :question/math-academy-id "q-11372" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{9x-38}{(4-x)^{2}(2-x)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{9x-38}{(4-x)^{2}(2-x)}=\\frac{A}{(4-x)}+\\frac{B}{(4-x)^{2}}+\\frac{C}{(2-x)}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,$ $B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(4-x)^{2}(2-x)$ and get\n\n$$\n9x-38=A(4-x)(2-x)+B(2-x)+C(4-x)^{2}.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=4,$ we can eliminate $A$ and $C$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9(4)-38 & =A(4-4)(2-4)+B(2-4)+C(4-4)^{2} \\\\ 36-38 & =B(-2) \\\\ B & =\\frac{-2}{-2} \\\\ B & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=2,$ we can eliminate $A$ and $B$ and solve for $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9(2)-38 & =A(4-2)(2-2)+B(2-2)+C(4-2)^{2} \\\\ 18-38 & =C{(2)}^{2} \\\\ C & =\\frac{-20}{4} \\\\ C & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=0$ and substituting the known values of $B$ and $C,$ we can solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9(0)-38 & =A(4-0)(2-0)+B(2-0)+C(4-0)^{2} \\\\ -38 & =8A+2B+16C \\\\ -38 & =8A+2(1)+16(-5) \\\\ -38 & =8A-78 \\\\ 8A & =78-38 \\\\ A & =\\frac{40}{8} \\\\ A & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{9x-38}{(4-x)^{2}(2-x)}=\\frac{5}{(4-x)}+\\frac{1}{(4-x)^{2}}-\\frac{5}{(2-x)}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{9x-38}{(4-x)^{2}(2-x)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{5}{(4-x)}+\\frac{1}{(4-x)^{2}}-\\frac{5}{(2-x)})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\int \\frac{1}{4-x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{(4-x)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x-5\\int \\frac{1}{2-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4-x|+\\frac{1}{4-x}+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2-x|+K,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K$ is an integral constant." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a1fdb08d-4e9a-5aa1-bf2f-9d236664e6fc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a1fdb08d-4e9a-5aa1-bf2f-9d236664e6fc" :answer-field/id #uuid "a1fdb08d-4e9a-5aa1-bf2f-9d236664e6fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-652ffd1d-a604-5671-a532-9fbbb91be568" :answer-field/choices ["answer-652ffd1d-a604-5671-a532-9fbbb91be568" "answer-3b89cb41-52b7-5666-8f50-16d233ce418c" "answer-bf74c85d-c2cb-5a97-9f09-4ade326e74d3" "answer-58923f50-9ab3-5f70-9ff3-7fb61c42ff32" "answer-0ab322b7-88c0-562d-aad6-28ae0e766ac0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-652ffd1d-a604-5671-a532-9fbbb91be568" :answer/id #uuid "652ffd1d-a604-5671-a532-9fbbb91be568" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4-x|+\\frac{1}{4-x}+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2-x|+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3b89cb41-52b7-5666-8f50-16d233ce418c" :answer/id #uuid "3b89cb41-52b7-5666-8f50-16d233ce418c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4-x|-\\frac{1}{4-x}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2-x|+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bf74c85d-c2cb-5a97-9f09-4ade326e74d3" :answer/id #uuid "bf74c85d-c2cb-5a97-9f09-4ade326e74d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4-x|+\\frac{5}{4-x}-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2-x|+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-58923f50-9ab3-5f70-9ff3-7fb61c42ff32" :answer/id #uuid "58923f50-9ab3-5f70-9ff3-7fb61c42ff32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4-x|-\\frac{5}{4-x}+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2-x|+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0ab322b7-88c0-562d-aad6-28ae0e766ac0" :answer/id #uuid "0ab322b7-88c0-562d-aad6-28ae0e766ac0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4-x|-\\frac{5}{4-x}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2-x|+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186184177 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0e54ebb5-b13c-5b43-a434-8a77b6f9b884"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-0e54ebb5-b13c-5b43-a434-8a77b6f9b884" :question/id #uuid "0e54ebb5-b13c-5b43-a434-8a77b6f9b884" :question/math-academy-id "q-75282" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent line to the polar curve $r=1-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ at $\\theta =\\pi ,$ given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(\\theta )=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ),\\,{x}^{′}(\\theta )=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the equation of the tangent line to a polar curve at a point $P,$ we follow four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Calculate the derivative $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}:$\n\nIn this case, we're given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(\\theta )=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ),\\,{x}^{′}(\\theta )=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{y}^{′}(\\theta )}{{x}^{′}(\\theta )} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )}{-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find the slope of the tangent at $P:$\n\nThe slope of the tangent line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{\\theta =\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )}{-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi )} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1-2\\cdot 0}{-0-2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1}{-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Find the Cartesian coordinates of $P:$\n\nWe compute the $xy$-coordinates of $P$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =(1-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =(1-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi )\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi  \\\\  & =(1-0)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-1 \\\\ {y}_{1} & =r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =(1-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =(1-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi )\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi  \\\\  & =(1-0)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of $P$ are $(-1,0).$\n\n**Step 4**: Using point-slope form, find the equation of the tangent:\n\nWe find the equation of the tangent as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-0 & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (x-(-1)) \\\\ y-0 & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (x+1) \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/70/7065086643b98b95b5d6face85544f33b00f73614a855fb9846ba68e5d987a33.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b589ba1a-614d-56c2-9925-d5bfb8d755e8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b589ba1a-614d-56c2-9925-d5bfb8d755e8" :answer-field/id #uuid "b589ba1a-614d-56c2-9925-d5bfb8d755e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-40e2a484-90cb-5f0c-a2b4-636fe404086d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7dcbe35b-5636-570d-b3cd-c1bd82df5118" "answer-eff134e1-d3ca-57b9-9c1d-9c3f3d2535e0" "answer-93c9e3b4-f68a-59e5-a47b-bd4f8b4df77a" "answer-40e2a484-90cb-5f0c-a2b4-636fe404086d" "answer-81c497bd-16b3-5f8b-936f-2a23c8ee0a74"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7dcbe35b-5636-570d-b3cd-c1bd82df5118" :answer/id #uuid "7dcbe35b-5636-570d-b3cd-c1bd82df5118" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eff134e1-d3ca-57b9-9c1d-9c3f3d2535e0" :answer/id #uuid "eff134e1-d3ca-57b9-9c1d-9c3f3d2535e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2x+\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-93c9e3b4-f68a-59e5-a47b-bd4f8b4df77a" :answer/id #uuid "93c9e3b4-f68a-59e5-a47b-bd4f8b4df77a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2}x+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-40e2a484-90cb-5f0c-a2b4-636fe404086d" :answer/id #uuid "40e2a484-90cb-5f0c-a2b4-636fe404086d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81c497bd-16b3-5f8b-936f-2a23c8ee0a74" :answer/id #uuid "81c497bd-16b3-5f8b-936f-2a23c8ee0a74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186233443 :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ef334055-d235-506e-a901-ee66a80f4e9e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ef334055-d235-506e-a901-ee66a80f4e9e" :answer-field/id #uuid "ef334055-d235-506e-a901-ee66a80f4e9e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8ba6070b-da1a-5e0b-a72d-fc13af7e3165" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1b339991-d53a-533c-8056-20f5d713d32d" "answer-8ba6070b-da1a-5e0b-a72d-fc13af7e3165" "answer-106587e7-d829-54ab-8b7e-609c77cf0a14" "answer-0ce64f0d-e9ba-5dbb-9ffc-282418bc0004" "answer-0afd21a9-c1f9-5631-b042-8d95195cced4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1b339991-d53a-533c-8056-20f5d713d32d" :answer/id #uuid "1b339991-d53a-533c-8056-20f5d713d32d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$L=0.$The series is convergent." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8ba6070b-da1a-5e0b-a72d-fc13af7e3165" :answer/id #uuid "8ba6070b-da1a-5e0b-a72d-fc13af7e3165" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$L=1.$ The root test gives no conclusion." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-106587e7-d829-54ab-8b7e-609c77cf0a14" :answer/id #uuid "106587e7-d829-54ab-8b7e-609c77cf0a14" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$L=1.$ The series is divergent." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0ce64f0d-e9ba-5dbb-9ffc-282418bc0004" :answer/id #uuid "0ce64f0d-e9ba-5dbb-9ffc-282418bc0004" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$L=3.$ The series is divergent." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0afd21a9-c1f9-5631-b042-8d95195cced4" :answer/id #uuid "0afd21a9-c1f9-5631-b042-8d95195cced4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$L=\\infty .$ The series is divergent." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186234032 :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0ebb4c90-61c1-5f3f-a84a-17bd726c40e3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0ebb4c90-61c1-5f3f-a84a-17bd726c40e3" :answer-field/id #uuid "0ebb4c90-61c1-5f3f-a84a-17bd726c40e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6a31fdad-f025-5641-a528-bd1d0f98c5b5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7dca9273-f96a-5ee0-a6d3-7e1206f51773" "answer-6859ef2c-19ed-5be4-a82c-9875ae292e49" "answer-6a31fdad-f025-5641-a528-bd1d0f98c5b5" "answer-97432ddb-a0a4-5e0b-91fb-38bf9a401171" "answer-588c52dd-f244-5cf8-bb03-52cf34b6c535"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7dca9273-f96a-5ee0-a6d3-7e1206f51773" :answer/id #uuid "7dca9273-f96a-5ee0-a6d3-7e1206f51773" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.3+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{43}{100}{(\\frac{1}{100})}^{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6859ef2c-19ed-5be4-a82c-9875ae292e49" :answer/id #uuid "6859ef2c-19ed-5be4-a82c-9875ae292e49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.3+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{43}{100}{(\\frac{1}{10})}^{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6a31fdad-f025-5641-a528-bd1d0f98c5b5" :answer/id #uuid "6a31fdad-f025-5641-a528-bd1d0f98c5b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.3+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{43}{10}{(\\frac{1}{100})}^{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-97432ddb-a0a4-5e0b-91fb-38bf9a401171" :answer/id #uuid "97432ddb-a0a4-5e0b-91fb-38bf9a401171" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.3+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{43}{1\\,000}{(\\frac{1}{10})}^{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-588c52dd-f244-5cf8-bb03-52cf34b6c535" :answer/id #uuid "588c52dd-f244-5cf8-bb03-52cf34b6c535" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2.343}{10}{(\\frac{1}{100})}^{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186101458 :question/problem "Calculate \n${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{n}^{2}+5n+6}.$\n\n*Hint: Try to factor the denominator first.*" :question/worked-solution "First, factoring the denominator and using partial fractions, we can write the series as\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{n}^{2}+5n+6}=\\frac{1}{(n+2)(n+3)}=\\frac{1}{n+2}-\\frac{1}{n+3}.\n$$\n\nSo, our series can be written as\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(\\frac{1}{n+2}-\\frac{1}{n+3}).\n$$\n\nLet's now compute the first few partial sums:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}_{1} & =(\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\ {s}_{2} & =(\\frac{1}{3}-\\cancel{\\frac{1}{4}})+(\\cancel{\\frac{1}{4}}-\\frac{1}{5}) \\\\ {s}_{3} & =(\\frac{1}{3}-\\cancel{\\frac{1}{4}})+(\\cancel{\\frac{1}{4}}-\\cancel{\\frac{1}{5}})+(\\cancel{\\frac{1}{5}}-\\frac{1}{6}) \\\\ {s}_{4} & =(\\frac{1}{3}-\\cancel{\\frac{1}{4}})+(\\cancel{\\frac{1}{4}}-\\cancel{\\frac{1}{5}})+(\\cancel{\\frac{1}{5}}-\\cancel{\\frac{1}{6}})+(\\cancel{\\frac{1}{6}}-\\frac{1}{7})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that for each partial sum, we always end up canceling all terms except for the first and last terms. Therefore, the $N$th partial sum is\n\n$$\n{s}_{N}=\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{1}{N+3}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can determine the sum of the series by taking the limit of ${s}_{N}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{(n+2)(n+3)} & ={lim}_{N\\to \\infty }{s}_{N} \\\\  & ={lim}_{N\\to \\infty }(\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{1}{N+3}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{3}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186099909 :answer-field/correct 17592186099914 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186234373 :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7e7684e4-e06c-57a4-94c9-8c4065eb02cc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7e7684e4-e06c-57a4-94c9-8c4065eb02cc" :answer-field/id #uuid "7e7684e4-e06c-57a4-94c9-8c4065eb02cc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8a795631-2118-587a-9c52-e7fcae53626a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-83a8233c-86f1-5b7d-9702-f1ccf8ac79b6" "answer-8a795631-2118-587a-9c52-e7fcae53626a" "answer-7c5b7c2e-42ac-5c76-8d0e-167934a4ded1" "answer-fbdf9a26-5fa5-5299-b0b5-3847f5e53bf1" "answer-47ace125-1428-5370-906c-bbbbca66287f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-83a8233c-86f1-5b7d-9702-f1ccf8ac79b6" :answer/id #uuid "83a8233c-86f1-5b7d-9702-f1ccf8ac79b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "63" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a795631-2118-587a-9c52-e7fcae53626a" :answer/id #uuid "8a795631-2118-587a-9c52-e7fcae53626a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "64" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7c5b7c2e-42ac-5c76-8d0e-167934a4ded1" :answer/id #uuid "7c5b7c2e-42ac-5c76-8d0e-167934a4ded1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "70" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fbdf9a26-5fa5-5299-b0b5-3847f5e53bf1" :answer/id #uuid "fbdf9a26-5fa5-5299-b0b5-3847f5e53bf1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "72" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-47ace125-1428-5370-906c-bbbbca66287f" :answer/id #uuid "47ace125-1428-5370-906c-bbbbca66287f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "74" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064209 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-dc80cc6c-733b-50ec-85a0-e9f5b6f29bef"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-dc80cc6c-733b-50ec-85a0-e9f5b6f29bef" :question/id #uuid "dc80cc6c-733b-50ec-85a0-e9f5b6f29bef" :question/math-academy-id "q-73332" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{1}^{2}x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u={x}^{2}-1.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x\\,⟹\\,x\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\text{d}u}{2}.\n$$\n\nComputing our limits of integration, we get\n\n| **$x$** | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **$u$** | $0$ | $3$ |\n\nWe can now solve the integral using our new variable $u,$ remembering to use the new limits of integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\sqrt{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{(\\frac{2{u}^{3/2}}{3})|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & ={\\frac{{u}^{3/2}}{3}|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{{3}^{3/2}}{3}-\\frac{{0}^{3/2}}{3} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-eb85d00d-c4fb-5b35-911e-a717db9a9969"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-eb85d00d-c4fb-5b35-911e-a717db9a9969" :answer-field/id #uuid "eb85d00d-c4fb-5b35-911e-a717db9a9969" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2a76db44-e626-54e3-bb32-fdade55a01be" :answer-field/choices ["answer-719b0fe5-3c99-5cac-84f5-1fc289687dce" "answer-c50c3670-73c7-5cc3-9ccf-673bb3533570" "answer-35321656-4bd6-5396-805d-37ad3b680477" "answer-2a76db44-e626-54e3-bb32-fdade55a01be" "answer-c52c231c-1dfb-55b4-9960-d0a4177ddef9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-719b0fe5-3c99-5cac-84f5-1fc289687dce" :answer/id #uuid "719b0fe5-3c99-5cac-84f5-1fc289687dce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c50c3670-73c7-5cc3-9ccf-673bb3533570" :answer/id #uuid "c50c3670-73c7-5cc3-9ccf-673bb3533570" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-35321656-4bd6-5396-805d-37ad3b680477" :answer/id #uuid "35321656-4bd6-5396-805d-37ad3b680477" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2a76db44-e626-54e3-bb32-fdade55a01be" :answer/id #uuid "2a76db44-e626-54e3-bb32-fdade55a01be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c52c231c-1dfb-55b4-9960-d0a4177ddef9" :answer/id #uuid "c52c231c-1dfb-55b4-9960-d0a4177ddef9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096720 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-881af2f1-aaf5-5e5d-a46a-df43ce3ea5ee"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-881af2f1-aaf5-5e5d-a46a-df43ce3ea5ee" :question/id #uuid "881af2f1-aaf5-5e5d-a46a-df43ce3ea5ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-84409" :question/problem "Kevin is moving his car in a straight line. His position relative to a fixed origin $O$ is given by the function $x(t)=2{e}^{t/2}\\,\\text{m},$ where $t$ is the time in seconds. Find its average position between $2$ and $6$ seconds." :question/worked-solution "To calculate the average value of the position on $[{t}_{1},{t}_{2}],$ we use the average value formula\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{{t}_{2}-{t}_{1}}\\,{\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}x(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{6-2}\\,{\\int }_{2}^{6}2{e}^{t/2}\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot {2\\cdot 2({e}^{t/2})|}_{2}^{6} \\\\  & ={e}^{6/2}-{e}^{2/2} \\\\  & ={e}^{3}-e.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average position is $({e}^{3}-e)\\,\\text{m}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8eb043c2-db7d-5e14-932d-20ffb968ecb7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8eb043c2-db7d-5e14-932d-20ffb968ecb7" :answer-field/id #uuid "8eb043c2-db7d-5e14-932d-20ffb968ecb7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0698e6b3-8baf-5fb0-aa2a-7fc2dc6f1d50" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0698e6b3-8baf-5fb0-aa2a-7fc2dc6f1d50" "answer-e1aa870a-ac3e-585f-bd93-cba436328789" "answer-3fa7013a-d3ff-5ede-95fd-816455406c82" "answer-51c95b82-1f8c-5ba4-b17a-3dfc2ef2f170" "answer-7dae70a2-67bf-5104-822e-1f7ffe60190e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0698e6b3-8baf-5fb0-aa2a-7fc2dc6f1d50" :answer/id #uuid "0698e6b3-8baf-5fb0-aa2a-7fc2dc6f1d50" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({e}^{3}-e)\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e1aa870a-ac3e-585f-bd93-cba436328789" :answer/id #uuid "e1aa870a-ac3e-585f-bd93-cba436328789" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({e}^{6}-{e}^{2})\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3fa7013a-d3ff-5ede-95fd-816455406c82" :answer/id #uuid "3fa7013a-d3ff-5ede-95fd-816455406c82" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4({e}^{3}-e)\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-51c95b82-1f8c-5ba4-b17a-3dfc2ef2f170" :answer/id #uuid "51c95b82-1f8c-5ba4-b17a-3dfc2ef2f170" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{3}-e)\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7dae70a2-67bf-5104-822e-1f7ffe60190e" :answer/id #uuid "7dae70a2-67bf-5104-822e-1f7ffe60190e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{6}-{e}^{2})\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068790 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d18dd5ed-e185-5cfc-926d-0d7b2a92c6df"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-d18dd5ed-e185-5cfc-926d-0d7b2a92c6df" :question/id #uuid "d18dd5ed-e185-5cfc-926d-0d7b2a92c6df" :question/math-academy-id "q-120180" :question/problem "Consider the finite region bounded by the curve $y=\\sqrt{x+2}$ and the $y$-axis from $y=2$ to $y=3.$ Which integral gives the volume of the solid generated when that region is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $y$-axis?" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the solid generated when the region bounded by a curve $x=g(y),$ the $y$-axis, and the horizontal lines $y=c$ and $y=d$ is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\nV=\\pi {\\int }_{c}^{d}[g(y)]^{2}\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write our equation in terms of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\sqrt{x+2} \\\\ {y}^{2} & =x+2 \\\\ x & ={y}^{2}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in our example, $g(y)={y}^{2}-2$ and the limits of integration are from $y=2$ to $y=3.$\n\nFinally, the volume can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =\\pi {\\int }_{c}^{d}{[g(y)]}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\pi {\\int }_{2}^{3}{({y}^{2}-2)}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\pi {\\int }_{2}^{3}({y}^{4}-4{y}^{2}+4)\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-315a9bb0-48e8-569d-b07b-4a5644ec8264"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-315a9bb0-48e8-569d-b07b-4a5644ec8264" :answer-field/id #uuid "315a9bb0-48e8-569d-b07b-4a5644ec8264" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b00ae438-d1aa-56bc-a2ef-bf52d2a89e7e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1ff669d2-de06-56d8-8f5c-68854882692a" "answer-73899ae8-32a9-5454-8013-2a30e4d6ada0" "answer-b00ae438-d1aa-56bc-a2ef-bf52d2a89e7e" "answer-a8cf2f80-e040-50b1-b53d-f4326f54cb9b" "answer-1432bb9a-ce4a-5f69-bb3d-d3b5455ac973"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1ff669d2-de06-56d8-8f5c-68854882692a" :answer/id #uuid "1ff669d2-de06-56d8-8f5c-68854882692a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi {\\int }_{2}^{3}(y+2)\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-73899ae8-32a9-5454-8013-2a30e4d6ada0" :answer/id #uuid "73899ae8-32a9-5454-8013-2a30e4d6ada0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi {\\int }_{2}^{3}({y}^{2}-2)\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b00ae438-d1aa-56bc-a2ef-bf52d2a89e7e" :answer/id #uuid "b00ae438-d1aa-56bc-a2ef-bf52d2a89e7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi {\\int }_{2}^{3}({y}^{4}-4{y}^{2}+4)\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a8cf2f80-e040-50b1-b53d-f4326f54cb9b" :answer/id #uuid "a8cf2f80-e040-50b1-b53d-f4326f54cb9b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{2}^{3}({y}^{2}-2)\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1432bb9a-ce4a-5f69-bb3d-d3b5455ac973" :answer/id #uuid "1432bb9a-ce4a-5f69-bb3d-d3b5455ac973" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{2}^{3}({y}^{4}-4{y}^{2}+4)\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064261 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-33a96099-4464-57a6-87f9-11f8046b2b50"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-33a96099-4464-57a6-87f9-11f8046b2b50" :question/id #uuid "33a96099-4464-57a6-87f9-11f8046b2b50" :question/math-academy-id "q-122387" :question/problem "![](images/b8/b8e332d7f53868313cc589e4ce5e991d2bcce88d15613111c4d0f920b678830d.png)\n\nWhich expression gives the total finite area enclosed between the curves $x={y}^{4}$ and $x={y}^{2},$ as shown above?\n\n*(Note: Figure not drawn to scale)*" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(y)={y}^{4}$ and $g(y)={y}^{2}.$ First, we find the intersections of the two curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(y) & =g(y) \\\\ {y}^{4} & ={y}^{2} \\\\ {y}^{4}-{y}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2}({y}^{2}-1) & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2}(y-1)(y+1) & =0 \\\\ y & =-1,0,1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area we want consists of two regions: ${A}_{1}$ and ${A}_{2}.$\n\n![](images/8b/8b4cbf07b9c2a6d949a58f39489889d2a3fdd4690664e530386f6f61d9aac5fd.png)\n\n- For the area ${A}_{1},$ we have $y\\in [-1,0],$ and the right function is $g(y)$ while the left function is $f(y).$ So, the area is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}(g(y)-f(y))\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}({y}^{2}-{y}^{4})\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the area ${A}_{2},$ we have $y\\in [0,1],$ and the right function is $g(y)$ while the left function is $f(y).$ So, the area is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(g(y)-f(y))\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{2}-{y}^{4})\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={A}_{1}+{A}_{2}={\\int }_{-1}^{0}({y}^{2}-{y}^{4})\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{2}-{y}^{4})\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bfc1653c-6513-5ab7-95f5-3af895b0238c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bfc1653c-6513-5ab7-95f5-3af895b0238c" :answer-field/id #uuid "bfc1653c-6513-5ab7-95f5-3af895b0238c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e55803c6-1d95-5033-92aa-8a0607c42665" :answer-field/choices ["answer-708792b5-dc3b-5780-9f52-2c74e75a789f" "answer-e55803c6-1d95-5033-92aa-8a0607c42665" "answer-c6423a8b-a7b1-5897-84f4-54bf126d2b03" "answer-5e15c88f-073f-51b7-975c-10a55ae55f2e" "answer-a5326780-633d-5ab5-b3dc-89a0af570ddd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-708792b5-dc3b-5780-9f52-2c74e75a789f" :answer/id #uuid "708792b5-dc3b-5780-9f52-2c74e75a789f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}({y}^{2}-y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}(y+{y}^{4})\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e55803c6-1d95-5033-92aa-8a0607c42665" :answer/id #uuid "e55803c6-1d95-5033-92aa-8a0607c42665" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}({y}^{2}-{y}^{4})\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{2}-{y}^{4})\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c6423a8b-a7b1-5897-84f4-54bf126d2b03" :answer/id #uuid "c6423a8b-a7b1-5897-84f4-54bf126d2b03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}({y}^{2}-{y}^{4})\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{4}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5e15c88f-073f-51b7-975c-10a55ae55f2e" :answer/id #uuid "5e15c88f-073f-51b7-975c-10a55ae55f2e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}({y}^{2}-{y}^{4})\\,\\text{d}y-{\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{2}-{y}^{4})\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a5326780-633d-5ab5-b3dc-89a0af570ddd" :answer/id #uuid "a5326780-633d-5ab5-b3dc-89a0af570ddd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}({y}^{2}+{y}^{4})\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096731 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8222fa21-5fa3-52f1-a894-4b100aeb534d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8222fa21-5fa3-52f1-a894-4b100aeb534d" :question/id #uuid "8222fa21-5fa3-52f1-a894-4b100aeb534d" :question/math-academy-id "q-10207" :question/problem "![](images/d4/d4bcdb6515b262c070c7ed689263efbbde8a350ad6a28b4fc106de281e69ff46.png)\n\nFind the area bounded between the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=2t,\\,y=t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\n$$\n\nand the $x$-axis for $t\\in [0,\\pi ].$" :question/worked-solution "The unsigned area bounded by the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=x(t),\\,y=y(t),\\,{t}_{1}\\le t\\le {t}_{2}\n$$\n\nand the $x$-axis is given by the absolute value of the integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}y\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain the integral expression\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}y\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that this integral will give us a positive number since $y\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\ge 0$ for all $t\\in [0,\\pi ].$\n\nTo solve the above integral, we use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=t & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & ⇒ & v=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t & =2t(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }-2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)(1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }+2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }+2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =-2(\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -0\\operatorname{cos}⁡0)+2(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}⁡0) \\\\  & =-2\\pi (-1) \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9aa35e99-bfe0-504f-b448-591e82ea534a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9aa35e99-bfe0-504f-b448-591e82ea534a" :answer-field/id #uuid "9aa35e99-bfe0-504f-b448-591e82ea534a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-74015f70-4e31-59fa-a156-c84a3e6516a2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-74015f70-4e31-59fa-a156-c84a3e6516a2" "answer-47e00196-5dc7-5e37-af21-0f88f4308a05" "answer-64e1b1f8-db18-57e8-b34a-cb959e797fd3" "answer-a27a6cf4-0fa2-53b5-9118-7c658d9dc6a5" "answer-91fc8920-5d08-5ae8-a052-34304d316f19"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-74015f70-4e31-59fa-a156-c84a3e6516a2" :answer/id #uuid "74015f70-4e31-59fa-a156-c84a3e6516a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-47e00196-5dc7-5e37-af21-0f88f4308a05" :answer/id #uuid "47e00196-5dc7-5e37-af21-0f88f4308a05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-64e1b1f8-db18-57e8-b34a-cb959e797fd3" :answer/id #uuid "64e1b1f8-db18-57e8-b34a-cb959e797fd3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a27a6cf4-0fa2-53b5-9118-7c658d9dc6a5" :answer/id #uuid "a27a6cf4-0fa2-53b5-9118-7c658d9dc6a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-91fc8920-5d08-5ae8-a052-34304d316f19" :answer/id #uuid "91fc8920-5d08-5ae8-a052-34304d316f19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105923 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-46e4a876-e7eb-598f-bbec-ff44b3be1391"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-46e4a876-e7eb-598f-bbec-ff44b3be1391" :question/id #uuid "46e4a876-e7eb-598f-bbec-ff44b3be1391" :question/math-academy-id "q-118775" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{1+4{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We break up the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{1+4{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{2}{1+4{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{1+4{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nEvaluating the first of these integrals, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{2}{1+4{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =2{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{0}\\frac{1}{1+4{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{0}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x){|}_{a}^{0}) \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡0-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2a)) \\\\  & =0-(-\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the integrand is an **even** function. This means that we can immediately deduce that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{1+4{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, since both improper integrals exist, we conclude that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{1+4{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{2}{1+4{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{1+4{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e62dccaf-73d1-5442-9e53-eebdcd332113"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e62dccaf-73d1-5442-9e53-eebdcd332113" :answer-field/id #uuid "e62dccaf-73d1-5442-9e53-eebdcd332113" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e5fa9767-9f89-5829-885f-cdf43d1a2b7d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-326e86ac-4b4d-58bd-bac0-9dc086c029d4" "answer-0d126f60-c244-55e8-99ea-c6908268f2e2" "answer-bcc743be-6c0f-592e-bc22-3ef4125c7e4d" "answer-e5fa9767-9f89-5829-885f-cdf43d1a2b7d" "answer-1a86b6cb-7dc9-57c4-8aaa-4c6993228125"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-326e86ac-4b4d-58bd-bac0-9dc086c029d4" :answer/id #uuid "326e86ac-4b4d-58bd-bac0-9dc086c029d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0d126f60-c244-55e8-99ea-c6908268f2e2" :answer/id #uuid "0d126f60-c244-55e8-99ea-c6908268f2e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bcc743be-6c0f-592e-bc22-3ef4125c7e4d" :answer/id #uuid "bcc743be-6c0f-592e-bc22-3ef4125c7e4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e5fa9767-9f89-5829-885f-cdf43d1a2b7d" :answer/id #uuid "e5fa9767-9f89-5829-885f-cdf43d1a2b7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1a86b6cb-7dc9-57c4-8aaa-4c6993228125" :answer/id #uuid "1a86b6cb-7dc9-57c4-8aaa-4c6993228125" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The integral diverges" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166798 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-cef928b3-a5b9-5b14-83bc-17bf537996f2"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-cef928b3-a5b9-5b14-83bc-17bf537996f2" :question/id #uuid "cef928b3-a5b9-5b14-83bc-17bf537996f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-96454" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{{tanh}^{2}⁡(3x-2)}{3}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the secant-tangent identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic secant-tangent identity:\n\n$$\n1-{tanh}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sech}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nSetting $\\theta =3x-2,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-{tanh}^{2}⁡(3x-2) & ={sech}^{2}⁡(3x-2) \\\\ {tanh}^{2}⁡(3x-2) & =1-{sech}^{2}⁡(3x-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{tanh}^{2}⁡(3x-2)}{3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int (1-{sech}^{2}⁡(3x-2))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int 1\\cdot \\text{d}x-\\frac{1}{3}\\int {sech}^{2}⁡(3x-2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(3x-2)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-faa2ee71-4e17-514a-a333-0d36f72cde02"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-faa2ee71-4e17-514a-a333-0d36f72cde02" :answer-field/id #uuid "faa2ee71-4e17-514a-a333-0d36f72cde02" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-27f4d9d3-7e96-5c12-b5a3-f9372b87c8d3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2710d395-2b8f-5a9c-8242-b8a14e7e70c8" "answer-07656df9-a2d3-55b7-968e-e7475835e5c3" "answer-27f4d9d3-7e96-5c12-b5a3-f9372b87c8d3" "answer-ca4bdf40-3643-5dc6-b993-f92752eaaf5c" "answer-b4fa43a8-904c-5b53-a2e7-0be8f2877828"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2710d395-2b8f-5a9c-8242-b8a14e7e70c8" :answer/id #uuid "2710d395-2b8f-5a9c-8242-b8a14e7e70c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3x-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(3x-2)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-07656df9-a2d3-55b7-968e-e7475835e5c3" :answer/id #uuid "07656df9-a2d3-55b7-968e-e7475835e5c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3x-\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(3x-2)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-27f4d9d3-7e96-5c12-b5a3-f9372b87c8d3" :answer/id #uuid "27f4d9d3-7e96-5c12-b5a3-f9372b87c8d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(3x-2)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ca4bdf40-3643-5dc6-b993-f92752eaaf5c" :answer/id #uuid "ca4bdf40-3643-5dc6-b993-f92752eaaf5c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{3}-\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(3x-2)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b4fa43a8-904c-5b53-a2e7-0be8f2877828" :answer/id #uuid "b4fa43a8-904c-5b53-a2e7-0be8f2877828" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(3x-2)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096765 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7bcaaf90-d33e-5a2f-9583-78877f436c71"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-7bcaaf90-d33e-5a2f-9583-78877f436c71" :question/id #uuid "7bcaaf90-d33e-5a2f-9583-78877f436c71" :question/math-academy-id "q-50330" :question/problem "![](images/31/31d4236bf58cd579c49c7259c32a2a9171e07c771b4c34040ac92896809f695f.png)\n\nThe region enclosed by the curves $x=\\frac{2}{y}$ and $x=3-y$ is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the line $x=-2.$ Which of the following gives the volume of the resulting solid?" :question/worked-solution "First, we want to determine the limits of integration. We find the intersections of the curves by solving the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{y} & =3-y \\\\ 2 & =3y-{y}^{2} \\\\ {y}^{2}-3y+2 & =0 \\\\ (y-1)(y-2) & =0 \\\\ y & =1,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, our limits of integration are from $y=1$ to $y=2.$\n\nNow, let's draw a horizontal arrow through the given region. The arrow should be pointing away from the axis of rotation.\n\n![](images/b7/b73c341f4d09b1df7bea162bc7dbe10d0ee60920c847f9c24210386a3d139e61.png)\n\nThe horizontal arrow \n\n- *enters* the region through the inner curve $x=\\frac{2}{y},$ and\n\n- *leaves* through the outer curve $x=3-y.$\n\nNext, we can find the volume of our solid as the difference between the volumes of the solids generated by the outer and inner curves.\n\n- **Step I.** Figure out the volume generated by the outer curve $x=3-y.$\n\n![](images/c8/c8c8e766c66e47a54f316f54893d603b245acec8f529da3a5033d2bba547a319.png)\n\nThe corresponding volume is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{V}_{\\text{outer}} & =\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{2}[\\,(\\text{right})-(\\text{left})\\,]^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{2}[\\,(3-y)-(-2)\\,]^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{2}{[5-y]}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- **Step II.** Figure out the volume generated by the inner curve $x=\\frac{2}{y}.$\n\n![](images/1b/1b31331f1c0da353bee6fe29d10e9e58dd531cbc8152cbce214d1adea771b032.png)\n\nThe corresponding volume is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{V}_{\\text{inner}} & =\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{2}[\\,(\\text{right})-(\\text{left})\\,]^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{2}{[\\,(\\frac{2}{y})-(-2)\\,]}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{2}{[\\frac{2}{y}+2]}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- **Step III.** Find the difference.\n\nFinally, we can write the volume of the original solid as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={V}_{\\text{outer}}-{V}_{\\text{inner}} \\\\  & =\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{2}{[5-y]}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y-\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{2}{[\\frac{2}{y}+2]}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{2}({[5-y]}^{2}-{[\\frac{2}{y}+2]}^{2})\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-24a6b34c-6b2b-59cf-97a5-55f1d3c4912c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-24a6b34c-6b2b-59cf-97a5-55f1d3c4912c" :answer-field/id #uuid "24a6b34c-6b2b-59cf-97a5-55f1d3c4912c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d10abc45-5b7c-5d5e-9462-2d886e2f6bc4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d30b7d3d-0dea-5470-83f6-553983d20016" "answer-7023af54-631a-5dcf-bf27-5f2705dfb93d" "answer-058cac9d-5a5a-5ee7-9198-6ebfb7207e0c" "answer-80f6d32e-5475-5dfc-9839-a9615e457aa0" "answer-d10abc45-5b7c-5d5e-9462-2d886e2f6bc4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d30b7d3d-0dea-5470-83f6-553983d20016" :answer/id #uuid "d30b7d3d-0dea-5470-83f6-553983d20016" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi {\\int }_{-2}^{-1}({[5-y]}^{2}-{[\\frac{2}{y}+2]}^{2})\\,\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7023af54-631a-5dcf-bf27-5f2705dfb93d" :answer/id #uuid "7023af54-631a-5dcf-bf27-5f2705dfb93d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{2}({[3-y]}^{2}-{[\\frac{2}{y}]}^{2})\\,\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-058cac9d-5a5a-5ee7-9198-6ebfb7207e0c" :answer/id #uuid "058cac9d-5a5a-5ee7-9198-6ebfb7207e0c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{2}({[5-y]}^{2}-{[\\frac{2}{y}+2]}^{2})\\,\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-80f6d32e-5475-5dfc-9839-a9615e457aa0" :answer/id #uuid "80f6d32e-5475-5dfc-9839-a9615e457aa0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{2}({[2+\\frac{2}{y}]}^{2})\\,\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d10abc45-5b7c-5d5e-9462-2d886e2f6bc4" :answer/id #uuid "d10abc45-5b7c-5d5e-9462-2d886e2f6bc4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{2}({[5-y]}^{2}-{[\\frac{2}{y}+2]}^{2})\\,\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186100932 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8deca7b4-0aaf-504b-958b-1e6e90c74a93"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8deca7b4-0aaf-504b-958b-1e6e90c74a93" :question/id #uuid "8deca7b4-0aaf-504b-958b-1e6e90c74a93" :question/math-academy-id "q-79877" :question/problem "![](images/49/49b119b378ac4f45c0c395ca77c5cefead3a7c811295b51ac8eaa8aef7100e25.png)\n\nThe base of a solid is the region enclosed by the curves $y=1-{x}^{2}$ and $y=-1,$  as shown in the picture. Cross-sections perpendicular to the $x$-axis are rectangles. If the height of each rectangle is $2$ times the length of its base, which integral gives the volume of the solid?" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=1-{x}^{2}$ and $g(x)=-1.$\n\nFirst, we determine the limits of integration. To do that, we find the intersections of the two curves by setting the functions equal to one another and solving for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =g(x) \\\\ 1-{x}^{2} & =-1 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the limit of integration are $x=-\\sqrt{2}$ and $x=\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nNow, consider a cross-section at some point $x$, where $x\\in (-\\sqrt{2},\\sqrt{2})$,  and its projection on the $xy$-plane: \n\n![](images/0c/0c2a676ecc781a2a7a78870eb93ee9fbe5a89a7bd754a446231c6e3237f75831.png)\n\nThe base of the cross-section is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =|f(x)-g(x)| \\\\  & =|1-{x}^{2}-(-1)| \\\\  & =|2-{x}^{2}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of a rectangle is\n$A=bh.$\n  So, since we have $h=2b,$ the expression for the area of the cross-section is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A(x) & =bh \\\\  & =2{b}^{2} \\\\  & =2{(2-{x}^{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =8-8{x}^{2}+2{x}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now calculate the volume of the solid, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}A(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{2}}^{\\sqrt{2}}(8-8{x}^{2}+2{x}^{4})\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-aeff073f-a16e-5f3f-a31e-6729474c2b63"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-aeff073f-a16e-5f3f-a31e-6729474c2b63" :answer-field/id #uuid "aeff073f-a16e-5f3f-a31e-6729474c2b63" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-62786fe1-c6f9-56dd-98a5-068099524de1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9a613018-d415-54e6-ad9f-5b9ca3b555a0" "answer-42da8871-cac3-553a-8b22-b39bd40cd1cf" "answer-1ded8cec-6c65-5b45-902e-409cb9650433" "answer-130ca9ad-058c-5822-8dbf-2f9979837568" "answer-62786fe1-c6f9-56dd-98a5-068099524de1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9a613018-d415-54e6-ad9f-5b9ca3b555a0" :answer/id #uuid "9a613018-d415-54e6-ad9f-5b9ca3b555a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{2}}^{\\sqrt{2}}(2-{x}^{2})\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-42da8871-cac3-553a-8b22-b39bd40cd1cf" :answer/id #uuid "42da8871-cac3-553a-8b22-b39bd40cd1cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{2}}^{\\sqrt{2}}(4-{x}^{4})\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1ded8cec-6c65-5b45-902e-409cb9650433" :answer/id #uuid "1ded8cec-6c65-5b45-902e-409cb9650433" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{2}(8-4x+2{x}^{2})\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-130ca9ad-058c-5822-8dbf-2f9979837568" :answer/id #uuid "130ca9ad-058c-5822-8dbf-2f9979837568" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{2}}^{\\sqrt{2}}(4-4{x}^{2}+{x}^{4})\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-62786fe1-c6f9-56dd-98a5-068099524de1" :answer/id #uuid "62786fe1-c6f9-56dd-98a5-068099524de1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{2}}^{\\sqrt{2}}(8-8{x}^{2}+2{x}^{4})\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096821 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-15fdecd3-2bb4-5c94-a4a3-305e0c26984d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-15fdecd3-2bb4-5c94-a4a3-305e0c26984d" :question/id #uuid "15fdecd3-2bb4-5c94-a4a3-305e0c26984d" :question/math-academy-id "q-103902" :question/problem "Let $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ and let ${P}_{3}(x)$ be the third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)$ about $x=1.$ Use the Lagrange error bound to find an upper bound for the error when ${P}_{3}(x)$ is used to approximate $\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.$" :question/worked-solution "The Lagrange error bound states that an upper bound for the error ${R}_{3}$ obtained when using the third-degree Taylor polynomial ${P}_{3}$ to approximate $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n|{R}_{3}|\\le \\frac{M}{4!}|x-1{|}^{4},\n$$\n\nwhere $M$ is the maximum value of $|{f}^{(4)}(x)|$ on the interval between $a=1$ and $x=2.$ \n\nPlugging $x=2$ into the above formula gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{R}_{3}| & \\le \\frac{M}{4!}|2-1{|}^{4} \\\\ |{R}_{3}| & \\le \\frac{M}{24}|1{|}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find $M,$ we need to compute $|{f}^{(4)}(x)|$ and then maximize it on the interval $[1,2].$ Taking the derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}} \\\\ {f}^{(4)}(x) & =-\\frac{6}{{x}^{4}} \\\\ |{f}^{(4)}(x)| & =|-\\frac{6}{{x}^{4}}|=\\frac{6}{{x}^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $|{f}^{(4)}(x)|=\\frac{6}{{x}^{4}}$ is a decreasing function in the interval $[1,2],$  its value is greatest at $x=1.$ So\n\n$$\nM=|{f}^{(4)}(1)|=\\frac{6}{(1)^{4}}=6,\n$$\n\nand therefore, the upper bound is\n\n$$\n|{R}_{3}|\\le \\frac{6}{24}|1{|}^{4}=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3dee6e17-9565-5642-81b9-7791c50bb056"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3dee6e17-9565-5642-81b9-7791c50bb056" :answer-field/id #uuid "3dee6e17-9565-5642-81b9-7791c50bb056" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-94817e0a-ff61-5937-8f82-4fdc78a55f96" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7ed1b7ea-f020-53de-ba57-6c7fa5462de6" "answer-94817e0a-ff61-5937-8f82-4fdc78a55f96" "answer-0adf5f03-f503-5641-88e2-3fce055cb3d3" "answer-aa41cea0-7e1a-565b-94bf-91ca37c53552" "answer-f2239c74-dc79-5d0e-a6f7-211e1208eaa6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7ed1b7ea-f020-53de-ba57-6c7fa5462de6" :answer/id #uuid "7ed1b7ea-f020-53de-ba57-6c7fa5462de6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|{R}_{3}|\\le \\frac{1}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-94817e0a-ff61-5937-8f82-4fdc78a55f96" :answer/id #uuid "94817e0a-ff61-5937-8f82-4fdc78a55f96" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|{R}_{3}|\\le \\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0adf5f03-f503-5641-88e2-3fce055cb3d3" :answer/id #uuid "0adf5f03-f503-5641-88e2-3fce055cb3d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|{R}_{3}|\\le \\frac{1}{64}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aa41cea0-7e1a-565b-94bf-91ca37c53552" :answer/id #uuid "aa41cea0-7e1a-565b-94bf-91ca37c53552" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|{R}_{3}|\\le \\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f2239c74-dc79-5d0e-a6f7-211e1208eaa6" :answer/id #uuid "f2239c74-dc79-5d0e-a6f7-211e1208eaa6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|{R}_{3}|\\le \\frac{3}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068801 :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Definite Integral of an Exponential-Trigonometric Expression Using Integration by Parts" :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078504 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-743918b2-4124-5be2-a1fd-716500b8cb35"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-743918b2-4124-5be2-a1fd-716500b8cb35" :question/id #uuid "743918b2-4124-5be2-a1fd-716500b8cb35" :question/math-academy-id "q-83470" :question/problem "The acceleration $a$ at time $t$ of a particle $P$ moving in the $xy$-plane is given by\n\n$$\na(t)=⟨4{e}^{2t},\\,9{e}^{3t}⟩.\n$$\n\nGiven that the particle is at the position $(1,1)$ and has velocity $⟨2,4⟩$ when $t=0,$ calculate the position vector of $P$ at time $t.$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the position vector, we need to integrate the velocity vector. To find the velocity vector, we first need to integrate the acceleration vector. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int ⟨4{e}^{2t},\\,9{e}^{3t}⟩\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨\\int 4{e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\int 9{e}^{3t}\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2{e}^{2t}+{C}_{1},\\,3{e}^{3t}+{C}_{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve for the constants of integration using the fact that $v(0)=⟨2,4⟩.$ Substituting $t=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(0) & =⟨2{e}^{2(0)}+{C}_{1},\\,3{e}^{3(0)}+{C}_{2}⟩ \\\\ ⟨2,4⟩ & =⟨2+{C}_{1},3+{C}_{2}⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso we must have ${C}_{1}=0$ and ${C}_{2}=1.$ Therefore, the velocity vector is\n\n$$\nv(t)=⟨2{e}^{2t},\\,3{e}^{3t}+1⟩.\n$$\n\nWe can compute the position vector by integrating the velocity vector.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int ⟨2{e}^{2t},\\,3{e}^{3t}+1⟩\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨\\int 2{e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\int (3{e}^{3t}+1)\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{2t}+{C}_{3},\\,{e}^{3t}+t+{C}_{4}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve for the constants of integration using the fact that $r(0)=⟨1,1⟩.$ Substituting $t=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(0) & =⟨{e}^{2(0)}+{C}_{3},\\,{e}^{3(0)}+0+{C}_{4}⟩ \\\\ ⟨1,1⟩ & =⟨1+{C}_{3},\\,1+{C}_{4}⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso we must have ${C}_{3}={C}_{4}=0.$ Therefore, the position of $P$ at time $t$ is\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨{e}^{2t},\\,{e}^{3t}+t⟩.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6c828a93-5ad8-5389-8e1d-dff274396206"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6c828a93-5ad8-5389-8e1d-dff274396206" :answer-field/id #uuid "6c828a93-5ad8-5389-8e1d-dff274396206" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-42a2d5bf-263e-583b-b1ce-d84d778a3c03" :answer-field/choices ["answer-dde445ba-ab44-5a01-ae5f-f82976b094fc" "answer-1424cef7-112d-5fb2-a1e4-a43f08ef3ec0" "answer-86b5677b-1c5e-54d1-88ed-d310ea17fadc" "answer-18cfd146-d9b1-5fc7-8a5a-7d89b8a8d28d" "answer-42a2d5bf-263e-583b-b1ce-d84d778a3c03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dde445ba-ab44-5a01-ae5f-f82976b094fc" :answer/id #uuid "dde445ba-ab44-5a01-ae5f-f82976b094fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r(t)=⟨2{e}^{2t}+t,\\,{e}^{3t}+t⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1424cef7-112d-5fb2-a1e4-a43f08ef3ec0" :answer/id #uuid "1424cef7-112d-5fb2-a1e4-a43f08ef3ec0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r(t)=⟨2{e}^{2t},\\,3{e}^{3t}+{t}^{2}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-86b5677b-1c5e-54d1-88ed-d310ea17fadc" :answer/id #uuid "86b5677b-1c5e-54d1-88ed-d310ea17fadc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r(t)=⟨4{e}^{2t}+t,\\,9{e}^{3t}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-18cfd146-d9b1-5fc7-8a5a-7d89b8a8d28d" :answer/id #uuid "18cfd146-d9b1-5fc7-8a5a-7d89b8a8d28d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r(t)=⟨{e}^{2t}+{t}^{2},\\,{e}^{3t}+t⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-42a2d5bf-263e-583b-b1ce-d84d778a3c03" :answer/id #uuid "42a2d5bf-263e-583b-b1ce-d84d778a3c03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r(t)=⟨{e}^{2t},\\,{e}^{3t}+t⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179677 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ea94a739-28fe-50a1-b5d4-4f34307441cf"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-ea94a739-28fe-50a1-b5d4-4f34307441cf" :question/id #uuid "ea94a739-28fe-50a1-b5d4-4f34307441cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-83878" :question/problem "The rate of growth in the frog population $P(t)$ in a certain lake follows the logistic growth model\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.1P(5\\,000-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, in years. Find an expression for the frog population after $t$ years, given that there were $100$ frogs initially." :question/worked-solution "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nThe general solution to the logistic growth equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{a}{1+C{e}^{-akt}}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the constant of proportionality is $k=0.1,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=5\\,000.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{5\\,000}{1+C{e}^{-(5\\,000\\cdot 0.1)t}}=\\frac{5\\,000}{1+C{e}^{-500t}}.\n$$\n\nWe now substitute the initial condition $P(0)=100$ and solve for $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5\\,000}{1+C{e}^{-500\\cdot 0}} & =100 \\\\ 1+C & =\\frac{5\\,000}{100} \\\\ C & =50-1 \\\\  & =49.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{5\\,000}{1+49{e}^{-500t}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-93650186-de97-555d-ac5a-338706314d50"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-93650186-de97-555d-ac5a-338706314d50" :answer-field/id #uuid "93650186-de97-555d-ac5a-338706314d50" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6545848f-d1c2-504e-8ca0-db1a6d9c5bf2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-45171aca-4721-5992-a53f-a77770463cf4" "answer-62d90b2f-3cf4-56cb-8f20-42532d4a4769" "answer-d5a2f479-09b1-51f2-87cb-2b2921667209" "answer-6545848f-d1c2-504e-8ca0-db1a6d9c5bf2" "answer-1d341268-ff40-5ed3-af0b-b6a741ea7f59"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-45171aca-4721-5992-a53f-a77770463cf4" :answer/id #uuid "45171aca-4721-5992-a53f-a77770463cf4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{1\\,000}{1+49{e}^{-50t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-62d90b2f-3cf4-56cb-8f20-42532d4a4769" :answer/id #uuid "62d90b2f-3cf4-56cb-8f20-42532d4a4769" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{1\\,000}{1+4{e}^{-500t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d5a2f479-09b1-51f2-87cb-2b2921667209" :answer/id #uuid "d5a2f479-09b1-51f2-87cb-2b2921667209" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{1\\,000}{1+5{e}^{-500t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6545848f-d1c2-504e-8ca0-db1a6d9c5bf2" :answer/id #uuid "6545848f-d1c2-504e-8ca0-db1a6d9c5bf2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{5\\,000}{1+49{e}^{-500t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1d341268-ff40-5ed3-af0b-b6a741ea7f59" :answer/id #uuid "1d341268-ff40-5ed3-af0b-b6a741ea7f59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(t)=\\frac{5\\,000}{1+4{e}^{-50t}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-6e55aeb2-db41-50e1-8b8c-a30ee7439c07" :activity/id #uuid "6e55aeb2-db41-50e1-8b8c-a30ee7439c07" :activity/title "Calculus II: Placement Exam" :activity/t